            <ArticleTitle>Pediatric synchronous bilateral ovarian torsion: a case report and review of the literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e19-23</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jpedsurg.2011.08.024</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ovarian torsion is a surgical emergency that can present with a variety of symptoms and hence is difficult to diagnose. We present the first case of a pediatric synchronous bilateral ovarian torsion in ovaries without pathology and review its presentation, diagnosis, treatment, outcome, and the associated literature.</AbstractText>
